Z||000009||VISCERAL||10-25-2001||02:12 PM||||The headers are form west coast fiero for about 800. I have spare stock manifolds with shiny heat shields and y pipe that i can cover gray w/eastwood manifold paint for the 3800sc, for sale-make offer.<BR>Haltech e6gm goes for about 700, you can use them on most gm motors and they plug right in. A lot easier to use for a swap of anything and still get total control over it. Just plug in their harness to the engines sensors and program it then go. Later on adjust for for different mods on the fly while car is running. No more hop up chips. No piggybacking ecms. Goto the haltech link above to see what that model can control and give them or a dealer a call.||||reg||1
Z||000010||pontiacs4me||10-25-2001||04:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AgaricX:<BR><B>Hey Visceral, I have a 3800SC, but am in need of exhaust parts.<P>How much for the heat coated headers and y-pipe?  Are they self-made or bought?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Soon I will be building a custom set of headers and y pipe for my fiero, I could build you a set for much less than WCF's price.  How soon do you need them?<P>||||reg||1
